  "term": "Home Observation for Measurement of the Environment",
  "definition": "The Home Observation for Measurement of the Environment is an assessment tool used to evaluate aspects of the care environment for infants and toddlers in child care settings. In the source, it is treated as one of several instruments for measuring child care quality and examining its reliability and validity.",
